<style>
.deck{--paper:var(--surface);font-size:17px}.deck *{box-sizing:border-box}
.deck .slide{position:relative;aspect-ratio:16/9;background:var(--paper);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:16px;box-shadow:var(--shadow);padding:2.2em 2.6em;margin:0 0 1.6em;overflow:hidden;display:flex;flex-direction:column}
.deck .slide h1{font:800 3.4em/1.05 Georgia,serif;margin:.4em 0}.deck .slide h2{font:700 1.75em/1.2 Georgia,serif;margin:0 0 1em;border:0;padding:0}
.deck .slide-n{position:absolute;right:1em;bottom:.6em;font:600 .75em ui-monospace,monospace;color:var(--ink-2)}
.deck .kick{font:700 .8em ui-monospace,monospace;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--accent)}.deck .big{font-size:1.25em}
.deck .cover{display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center;height:100%}
.deck .tiles{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:.8em;margin:1em 0}.deck .tiles div{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:.8em 1em;color:var(--ink-2);font-size:.9em;background:var(--surface-2)}.deck .tiles b{display:block;font:800 2.3em/1.1 Georgia,serif;color:var(--ink)}
.deck .cap{color:var(--ink-2);font-size:.9em;margin:.4em 0 0}.deck ul,.deck ol{margin:.6em 0 0;padding-left:1.2em;font-size:1em}.deck li{margin:.3em 0}
.deck .two{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;grid-template-rows:minmax(0,1fr);gap:1em;min-height:0;flex:1 1 0}.deck .shot{margin:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;min-height:0;height:100%}
.deck .shot img{width:100%;flex:1 1 0;min-height:0;object-fit:cover;object-position:top;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px}.deck .shot figcaption{font-size:.8em;color:var(--ink-2);margin-top:.3em}
.deck .two+ul{font-size:.82em;margin-top:.5em;flex:none}
.deck .heat{width:100%}.deck .heat .hl{font:600 14px system-ui;fill:var(--ink)}.deck .heat .hx{font:11px ui-monospace,monospace;fill:var(--ink-2)}.deck .heat .nil{fill:var(--line)}
.deck .bars .b{display:grid;grid-template-columns:110px 1fr 40px;gap:.8em;align-items:center;margin:.35em 0}.deck .bars i{display:block;height:20px;border-radius:5px}
.deck .dotrow{display:grid;grid-template-columns:90px 22em 1fr;gap:.6em;align-items:center;margin:.5em 0}.deck .dotrow i{display:inline-block;width:22px;height:22px;border-radius:6px;margin-right:4px}.deck .dotrow em{font-style:normal;color:var(--ink-2);font-size:.85em}
.deck .keys{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:1em;margin:1em 0}.deck .keys .k{border:2px dashed var(--line-2);border-radius:14px;padding:1em;opacity:.6}.deck .keys .k.on{border:2px solid var(--c);opacity:1}.deck .keys b{display:block;font-size:1.3em}.deck .keys span{color:var(--ink-2)}
.deck .raci{border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.95em;width:100%}.deck .raci td,.deck .raci th{border:1px solid var(--line);padding:.35em .5em;text-align:center}.deck .raci td:first-child{text-align:left}
.deck .rA{background:var(--accent);color:var(--accent-ink);font-weight:800}.deck .rR{background:var(--accent-soft);font-weight:700}.deck .rC{color:var(--ink)}.deck .rI{color:var(--ink-2)}
.deck .three{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:1em;min-height:0;flex:1 1 0;overflow:hidden}.deck .three h3{margin:0 0 .3em;font-size:1em}.deck .pts{list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0;font-size:.72em}.deck .pts li{margin:.25em 0;padding-left:.5em;border-left:4px solid var(--line-2)}.deck .pts li.late{border-color:var(--warm)}.deck .pts li.today{border-color:var(--accent)}.deck .pts span{display:block;color:var(--ink-2)}.deck .decide li{font-size:1.1em;margin:.5em 0}
.deck.one .slide{display:none;margin:0}.deck.one .slide.current{display:flex}.deck.one>:not(.slide):not(.deck-bar){display:none}
.deck .deck-bar{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.5em;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:.8em 0 1.2em}.deck .deck-bar button,.deck .deck-pdf{font:inherit;font-size:.9em;font-weight:700;padding:.45em .9em;border-radius:10px;border:1px solid var(--line-2);background:var(--surface);color:var(--ink);cursor:pointer;text-decoration:none}
.deck .deck-bar [data-prev],.deck .deck-bar [data-next]{background:var(--accent);color:var(--accent-ink);border-color:var(--accent);min-width:3em}.deck .deck-bar button:disabled{opacity:.35;cursor:default}
.deck .deck-pos{font:600 .9em ui-monospace,monospace;min-width:4.5em;text-align:center}.deck .deck-gap{flex:1}
.deck.all .deck-bar{position:sticky;bottom:0;background:var(--bg);padding:.5em 0;margin:0}
.deck.full,.deck:fullscreen{position:fixed;inset:0;z-index:1000;background:var(--bg);display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;justify-content:center;padding:1vh 2vw;font-size:clamp(14px,1.45vw,26px)}
.deck.full .slide.current,.deck:fullscreen .slide.current{width:min(96vw,150vh)}.deck.full .deck-bar,.deck:fullscreen .deck-bar{width:min(96vw,150vh);margin:.6em 0 0}
html.deck-on body{overflow:hidden}
@media (max-width:760px){.deck .slide{aspect-ratio:auto;min-height:70vh;padding:1.1em;overflow:visible}.deck .two,.deck .tiles,.deck .keys,.deck .three{grid-template-columns:1fr}.deck .two{flex:none}.deck .shot img{flex:none;height:auto;max-height:45vh}
.deck .slide h1{font-size:2.2em}.deck .slide h2{font-size:1.35em}.deck .dotrow{grid-template-columns:5em 1fr}.deck .dotrow em{grid-column:1/-1}.deck .raci{font-size:.75em}.deck .bars .b{grid-template-columns:5em 1fr 2.5em}.deck .three{flex:none;overflow:visible}.deck .deck-gap{display:none}}
@media print{.deck .deck-bar{display:none}}
</style>
<div class="deck one" data-pdf="../../../assets/shows/2026-11-10-1600/deck.pdf"><section class="slide" aria-label="cover"><div class="cover"><p class="kick">RiskMandate · Web Summit Lisbon 2026</p><h1>Give agents access. Not free rein.</h1><p class="big">For security teams: know exactly what every agent can do, what it was allowed to do, and what really stops it. Shown on our own team of more than a hundred agents.</p><p class="cap">Every number and scenario here is on the public record (git, the sites, the ABP pages), 10 November 2026. Links on the last slide.</p></div></section><section class="slide" aria-label="The problem"><h2>Agents now have reach. Who decided what they may do with it?</h2><ul><li><b>Agents sit in Gmail, HR, payroll, the CRM and meeting apps,</b> with the same access their users have</li><li><b>Reach:</b> what an agent can actually do. <b>Mandate:</b> what the business authorised it to do. <b>The gap</b> between the two is the risk</li><li><b>Today the gap is invisible:</b> nobody can list each agent, its reach, its mandate and what really stops it</li><li><b>RiskMandate:</b> know their reach, define their mandate, control the gap (riskmandate.ai)</li></ul></section><section class="slide" aria-label="For the security team"><h2>A security must-have, not a compliance nice-to-have</h2><ul><li><b>Built for the security team,</b> the people who answer when an agent does something it should not</li><li><b>Their questions, answered per agent:</b> what can it reach? what was it allowed to do? what actually stops it? what did it try?</li><li><b>Evidence, not paperwork:</b> each barrier is labelled a rule, a review or a technical control, with the commit or log that shows it</li><li><b>Enforced where security already works:</b> the gateway, proxy or IAM they run, or SHarness on the machine the agent runs on</li><li><b>Compliance follows from it:</b> the same record answers the auditor and the insurer, as a by-product, not the product</li></ul></section><section class="slide" aria-label="RiskMandate"><h2>An Agent Behaviour Policy for every agent, enforced by the controls you already run</h2><div class="two"><figure class="shot"><img src="../../../assets/shows/2026-11-10-1600/riskmandate-controls.jpg" alt="riskmandate.ai: one ABP per agent; your gateway allows, redacts, holds or blocks" loading="lazy"><figcaption>riskmandate.ai: one ABP per agent; your gateway allows, redacts, holds or blocks</figcaption></figure><div><ul><li><b>The ABP</b> records each agent's reach, mandate, gap and the barrier that really stops it</li><li><b>Enforced</b> by your gateway, proxy or IAM, or SHarness, the open-source secure harness</li><li><b>Never in the request path:</b> RiskMandate writes the rules; your controls apply them</li><li><b>One record</b> read by operations, leadership, security and the insurer</li></ul></div></div></section><section class="slide" aria-label="Our own team"><h2>We run it on ourselves: nine people, 119 agents that have run, 85 at work in 48 hours</h2><figure class="shot"><img src="../../../assets/shows/2026-11-10-1600/angelo-live.jpg" alt="The team, live: each dot is an agent, each line a message between agents and people" loading="lazy"><figcaption>The team, live: each dot is an agent, each line a message between agents and people</figcaption></figure></section><section class="slide" aria-label="An ABP per agent"><h2>Every one of our agents has a published behaviour policy</h2><div class="two"><figure class="shot"><img src="../../../assets/shows/2026-11-10-1600/abp-index.jpg" alt="web-summit.sgit.ai/abp/: 93 pages, one per agent" loading="lazy"><figcaption>web-summit.sgit.ai/abp/: 93 pages, one per agent</figcaption></figure><div><ul><li><b>Reach, Mandate, Gap, Barrier</b> for every agent, each barrier labelled a rule, a review or a technical control, with the evidence</li><li><b>Explorer phase first:</b> observe and recommend, lock down step by step, always with an escape valve for a person</li><li><b>Then strict:</b> deny by default, with hooks that block what the policy denies</li><li><b>Kept by an agent</b> (abp@), reviewed hourly; security agents review every commit for keys, contact details and private data</li></ul></div></div></section><section class="slide" aria-label="The circuit"><h2>Every agent, through its policy and its barriers, to what it can touch</h2><figure class="shot"><img src="../../../assets/shows/2026-11-10-1600/silvio-circuit.jpg" alt="Silvio&#x27;s circuit, live: 109 agents, 94 with a written policy; each wired through its ABP and barriers to the resources it reaches" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Silvio&#x27;s circuit, live: 109 agents, 94 with a written policy; each wired through its ABP and barriers to the resources it reaches</figcaption></figure></section><section class="slide" aria-label="What the policies caught"><h2>What the policies caught in the first five days</h2><div class="two"><figure class="shot"><img src="../../../assets/shows/2026-11-10-1600/abp-in-action.jpg" alt="ABP in action: every scenario tied to its commit" loading="lazy"><figcaption>ABP in action: every scenario tied to its commit</figcaption></figure><div><ul><li><b>7 caught by a review</b> before they went out: a token about to be published, a stale key entry, a vault key printed into a transcript, a read key about to reach a model provider</li><li><b>7 found by an ABP</b> and fixed by their owner</li><li><b>1 rule failed and became a technical barrier:</b> "never push to main" did not hold once; main is now protected</li><li><b>The lesson:</b> rules alone failed once; reviews caught seven; every technical barrier we have was added after an ABP or a review named the gap</li></ul></div></div></section><section class="slide" aria-label="Watch it"><h2>Policies you can watch</h2><div class="two"><figure class="shot"><img src="../../../assets/shows/2026-11-10-1600/abp-player.jpg" alt="The ABP player: a policy in action, step by step" loading="lazy"><figcaption>The ABP player: a policy in action, step by step</figcaption></figure><div><ul><li><b>For the demo at the stand:</b> the same request with and without the policy, side by side</li><li><b>Try it in five minutes</b> on Claude or ChatGPT: paste one line that says the agent must not, and watch it refuse. That line is the first row of an ABP</li><li><b>Then the stronger barriers:</b> why a rule the agent keeps by choice is the weakest of the four</li></ul></div></div></section><section class="slide" aria-label="Measuring the market"><h2>GAMMA-Ray: how much an agent does on its own, and how well that is governed</h2><div class="two"><figure class="shot"><img src="../../../assets/shows/2026-11-10-1600/gamma-spectrum.jpg" alt="Seven Spectrum cards published (beta)" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Seven Spectrum cards published (beta)</figcaption></figure><figure class="shot"><img src="../../../assets/shows/2026-11-10-1600/gamma-lens.jpg" alt="The lens: what is said about an agent, what its grant lets it do, and the delta" loading="lazy"><figcaption>The lens: what is said about an agent, what its grant lets it do, and the delta</figcaption></figure></div><ul><li><b>One short set of questions</b> over 8 public maturity instruments and 279 provisions</li><li><b>Every agent product at the summit</b> can be scanned from public evidence: Replit, Manus, and ten Portuguese companies in review</li><li><b>RiskMandate's lens:</b> the grant measures what permissions let an agent do; the delta is the gap</li></ul></section><section class="slide" aria-label="Trust in each fact"><h2>FACT-Ray: how far to trust each fact behind a score</h2><div class="two"><figure class="shot"><img src="../../../assets/shows/2026-11-10-1600/fact-ray.jpg" alt="gamma-ray.sgit.ai/fact-ray/" loading="lazy"><figcaption>gamma-ray.sgit.ai/fact-ray/</figcaption></figure><div><ul><li><b>Who says it, how firmly it is recorded, who stands behind it:</b> trust, not truth</li><li><b>Companies answer for themselves</b> with one file on their own domain</li><li><b>The same discipline</b> we apply to our own agents' evidence</li></ul></div></div></section><section class="slide" aria-label="How we work"><h2>How the agentic team delivers: a voice brief in, a release out</h2><div class="two"><figure class="shot"><img src="../../../assets/shows/2026-11-10-1600/pipeline.jpg" alt="From a voice brief to TestFlight in 1 h 40, traced across five repositories" loading="lazy"><figcaption>From a voice brief to TestFlight in 1 h 40, traced across five repositories</figcaption></figure><div><ul><li><b>Every agent has its own key;</b> every commit names its agent; every push is a version that passed a gate</li><li><b>Only the operator instructs;</b> agents draft, people send; humans can stop or restart any agent</li><li><b>Since 2 November:</b> two sites (4,716 and 3,070 commits), a new standard and its site, apps on TestFlight, interviews published from the summit floor</li><li><b>The big stop:</b> every team paused in minutes, realigned and restarted, a live test of control</li></ul></div></div></section><section class="slide" aria-label="Why it matters"><h2>Why security teams need this now</h2><ul><li><b>Every company is about to run teams of agents</b> with real reach. Security teams will be asked what each one can do, and today they cannot answer</li><li><b>We already run such a team,</b> at speed, and show where the risk sits and what controls it</li><li><b>Our own team is the case study:</b> the scenarios, the failures and the fixes are public, each with its commit</li><li><b>An open approach:</b> the ABP model and SHarness are public; enforcement uses the controls customers already have</li><li><b>Next:</b> design partnerships with security teams; from explorer to strict policies with hooks; GAMMA-Ray scans of the agent products they buy</li></ul></section><section class="slide" aria-label="Live links"><h2>See it live</h2><ul><li><b>RiskMandate:</b> riskmandate.ai (the film, the six examples, "try it in five minutes")</li><li><b>Our ABPs:</b> web-summit.sgit.ai/abp/ · ABP in action: web-summit.sgit.ai/abp/in-action/</li><li><b>The circuit:</b> web-summit.sgit.ai/people/silvio/app/ then Universe, Circuit</li><li><b>The team, live:</b> web-summit.sgit.ai/people/angelo/app/#live</li><li><b>GAMMA-Ray:</b> gamma-ray.sgit.ai/spectrum/ · the lens: gamma-ray.sgit.ai/lens/ · FACT-Ray: gamma-ray.sgit.ai/fact-ray/</li></ul></section></div>
<script src="../../../assets/deck.js" defer></script>
